    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: However, in 785, wary of the customs his son may have been taking in Aquitaine,
    Charlemagne sent for him to Aquitaine and Louis presented himself at the Royal
    Council of Paderborn dressed up in Basque costumes along with other youths in
    the same garment, which may have made a good impression in Toulouse, since the
    Basques of Vasconia were a mainstay of the Aquitanian army.
