    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'Louis was crowned King of Aquitaine as a child in 781 and sent there with
    regents and a court. Charlemagne constituted the sub-kingdom in order to secure
    the border of his kingdom after the destructive war against the Aquitanians and
    Basques under Waifer (capitulated c. 768) and later Hunald II, which culminated
    in the disastrous Battle of Roncesvalles (778). '
